# nodes.ini - the fleet inventory, single source of truth for node names,
# hosts and roles. Copy this file to nodes.ini and replace every host= value
# with your own machines' addresses:
#
#   cp nodes.ini.example nodes.ini
#
# One node per line:
#
#   <name> host=<ip> role=validator|rpc [dc=<tag>]
#
# - name is the PRIMARY KEY everywhere: fleet verbs (./fleet up a1), the
#   staking key dir (staking/l1/<name>), the node-ids.env manifest and the
#   node's data root on its box (data/<name>). On a first run the names are
#   yours to pick; only edit host=. When restoring a 03_backup_secrets.sh
#   backup, the names MUST match the staking/l1/<name> dirs already in it.
# - host: the address the control host ssh'es to AND the node's --public-ip
#   that its peers dial. Validators are internal-only by design, so use their
#   DC-internal addresses.
# - role: validator (registered L1 validator; a "spare" is just a validator
#   at low on-chain weight) or rpc (tracks the chain, serves ingress, never
#   registered, never wears a BLS signer key).
# - dc is a display-only tag: `fleet status` groups by it and fleet verbs
#   accept dc=<tag> selectors. Nothing functional depends on it.
# - Weights are NOT inventory: `l1 create` registers every validator at a
#   constant initial weight of 1000; the real distribution (site A active,
#   site B standby) is applied via `l1 apply` / scenarios/00_healthy.sh and
#   the on-chain weight is the sole truth.
# - Ports are positional per host: the k-th node on a host serves HTTP on
#   9650+2k and staking p2p on 9651+2k (one node per host = 9650/9651).
#   Reordering nodes that share a host shifts the later nodes' ports:
#   redeploy that host's nodes after such an edit.

# --- DC A ----------------------------------------------------------------
a1     host=10.0.0.11  role=validator  dc=A
a2     host=10.0.0.12  role=validator  dc=A
a3     host=10.0.0.13  role=validator  dc=A
a4     host=10.0.0.14  role=validator  dc=A
rpc_a1 host=10.0.0.15  role=rpc        dc=A
rpc_a2 host=10.0.0.16  role=rpc        dc=A

# --- DC B ----------------------------------------------------------------
b1     host=10.1.0.11  role=validator  dc=B
b2     host=10.1.0.12  role=validator  dc=B
b3     host=10.1.0.13  role=validator  dc=B
b4     host=10.1.0.14  role=validator  dc=B
rpc_b1 host=10.1.0.15  role=rpc        dc=B
rpc_b2 host=10.1.0.16  role=rpc        dc=B
